                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "Introduced to avoid using dcterms:provenance for epistemic source-status annotations."@en ;
                                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www.dublincore.org/specifications/dublin-core/dcmi-terms/terms/provenance/> ;
                                      rdfs:comment "Annotation property used to state the epistemic or normative status of the source for an ontology resource, for example direct legal definition, explicit legal information element, ESPR-grounded modelling abstraction, or JRC draft proposal. It is intentionally distinct from dcterms:provenance, which is reserved for ownership and custody history."@en ;
