###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#SoCQualificationAssertion
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#SoCQualificationAssertion> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Article 2(27)."@en ;
                                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2006/1907/oj> ,
                                                                                     <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2008/1272/oj> ,
                                                                                     <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/1021/oj> ,
                                                                                     <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> ;
                                                   rdfs:comment "A documented, explicit assertion that a substance satisfies one or more non-exclusive qualification criteria in ESPR Article 2(27). For criterion (d), the applicable product context is represented by a dpp:SubstancePresence linked through dpp:hasApplicableQualification. This modelling construct records asserted qualification evidence; it does not infer legal status."@en ;
                                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> ;
                                                   rdfs:label "SoC qualification assertion"@en ;
                                                   <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "ESPR-grounded modelling construct for recording an explicit Article 2(27) qualification; the assertion is not itself a legal term and the ontology does not infer legal status."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "REACH Article 3(1)"@en ;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2006/1907/oj> ;
                                   rdfs:comment "A chemical substance used as the generic superclass for substance identity and naming information. In this SOC module it primarily supports the modelling of dpp:SubstanceOfConcern; its presence does not make SOC a general-purpose substance-reporting module."@en ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Substance"@en ;
                                   <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "direct legal definition reproduced from the cited legislation."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceManagementInstruction
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceManagementInstruction> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Article 7(5)(d)-(e)"@en ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "An instruction concerning the management of a substance of concern in its SubstancePresence context, including safe use, disassembly, preparation for reuse, reuse, recycling and environmentally sound end-of-life management. This domain-specific modelling abstraction supports the information elements in ESPR Article 7(5)(d)-(e); it is not a term defined by the Regulation and does not determine legal obligations or applicability."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Substance management instruction"@en ;
                                                        <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "ESPR-grounded ontology modelling abstraction; this RDF resource is not itself a term defined by the Regulation."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceOfConcern
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceOfConcern> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance> ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Article 2(27)"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A substance that: (a) meets the criteria laid down in Article 57 of Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 and is identified in accordance with Article 59(1) of that Regulation; (b) is classified in Part 3 of Annex VI to Regulation (EC) No 1272/2008 in one of the following hazard classes or hazard categories: (i) carcinogenicity categories 1 and 2; (ii) germ cell mutagenicity categories 1 and 2; (iii) reproductive toxicity categories 1 and 2; (iv) endocrine disruption for human health categories 1 and 2; (v) endocrine disruption for the environment categories 1 and 2; (vi) persistent, mobile and toxic or very persistent, very mobile properties; (vii) persistent, bioaccumulative and toxic or very persistent, very bioaccumulative properties; (viii) respiratory sensitisation category 1; (ix) skin sensitisation category 1; (x) hazardous to the aquatic environment — categories chronic 1 to 4; (xi) hazardous to the ozone layer; (xii) specific target organ toxicity — repeated exposure categories 1 and 2; (xiii) specific target organ toxicity — single exposure categories 1 and 2; (c) is regulated under Regulation (EU) 2019/1021; or (d) negatively affects the reuse and recycling of materials in the product in which it is present."@en ;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> ;
                                            rdfs:label "Substance of concern"@en ;
                                            <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "direct legal definition reproduced from the cited legislation."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstancePresence
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstancePresence> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "ESPR Article 7(5)(a)–(e)"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> ;
                                           rdfs:comment "A contextual relation entity representing the presence of a substance in relation to a product as placed on the market, including a product, component or spare part. It enables product-dependent location, concentration and instruction information to be represented without treating those data as intrinsic characteristics of the substance itself or classifying the presence as a product property. In the CORE profile the modelling pattern is one SubstancePresence per reported location when different locations require different concentrations; sector-specific extensions may provide explicit reference bases for several calculation perspectives. This class is an ontology modelling abstraction supporting ESPR Article 7(5), rather than a term explicitly defined by the Regulation."@en ;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> ;
                                           rdfs:label "Substance presence"@en ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "ESPR-grounded ontology modelling abstraction; this RDF resource is not itself a term defined by the Regulation."@en .


